WEBVTT

00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:01.113
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:13.697 --> 00:00:15.121
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> Do you like the book?

00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:18.274
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> Yes, I do. It’s very good.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.031
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> She’s my favourite writer.

00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:23.344
I love her books.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:27.897
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:30.121 --> 00:00:31.674
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> Do you live in New York?

00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:35.907
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> No, I don’t. I live in London.

00:00:36.157 --> 00:00:38.757
My husband and I work for a British company.

00:00:38.957 --> 00:00:39.638
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> Oh!

00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:41.360
Do you have children?

00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:43.216
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> No, we don’t.

00:00:43.406 --> 00:00:46.423
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> I have two sons and a daughter.

00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:51.308
David and Andrew are at university and Carla’s at school.

00:00:51.755 --> 00:00:54.304
Look. Here are some photos…

00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:58.005
This is a photo of our holiday in Barbados.

00:00:58.252 --> 00:00:59.699
Do you know Barbados?

00:01:00.313 --> 00:01:02.121
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> No, I don’t.

00:01:05.964 --> 00:01:06.912
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:01:09.158 --> 00:01:12.244
<v><b>Attendant:</b></v> Do you want meat, fish, or pasta?

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.017
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> Oh, fish, please.

00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.007
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> Pasta for me, please.

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:23.050
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> How’s your pasta?

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.793
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> It’s OK.

00:01:25.312 --> 00:01:27.307
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> This fish isn’t very good.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.832
Excuse me, I don’t like this fish.

00:01:32.147 --> 00:01:34.375
Can I have the pasta, please?

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.280
<v><b>Attendant:</b></v> I’m sorry, madam. It’s finished.

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:42.176
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:01:44.724 --> 00:01:46.981
<v><b>Eve:</b></v> Oh, I need to go to the toilet.

00:01:49.014 --> 00:01:50.857
Oops, sorry.

00:01:53.274 --> 00:01:56.492
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> Excuse me. What time do we arrive?

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.955
<v><b>Attendant:</b></v> In twenty-five minutes, madam.

00:01:59.691 --> 00:02:00.791
<v><b>Wendy:</b></v> That’s good!